The Syrian National Earthquake Center participated in an advanced workshop organized by the Arab Center for Earthquake and Natural Disaster Prevention, held in Algeria on November 11-12. The event, which centered on evaluating earthquake hazards, was a collaborative effort with the Global Earthquake Model (GEM) Foundation and brought together specialists from ten Arab nations.

Participants received training on the OpenQuake Engine software, learning to craft detailed seismic hazard models and generate risk maps to evaluate potential earthquake effects. Jamal Zakkour, leader of the National Earthquake Center, remarked that the workshop offered significant insights into how Algeria assesses earthquake risks and facilitated the sharing of expertise and contemporary methods among the involved nations. This collaboration enhanced the comprehension of seismic phenomena in the area and bolstered disaster response plans.

