On Boxing Day, Environment Canada issued blowing snow advisories for Alberta’s two largest cities, Calgary and the Edmonton area, due to extremely low visibility caused by the interplay of wind and precipitation. The weather agency warned that travel conditions could be perilous and urged motorists to avoid unnecessary journeys in affected regions until conditions improve.

The advisories are part of a broader set of winter weather alerts affecting various communities across the province. Environment Canada also announced alerts for snowfall and frigid temperatures in certain areas of Alberta, with residents in some locales advised to prepare for potentially blizzard-like conditions on Saturday.

