Bahan's situation is not unique. A 2024 report by the Professional Law Group indicates that between 26% and 50% of insurance claims in Florida were rejected following the hurricanes during the 2023-2024 period. Insurance companies are subtly raising deductibles to offset the surge in claims, a trend not limited to hurricanes. Californians also face the risk of rising insurance rates due to increased wildfire risks.

The amplified severity of weather phenomena is likely attributable to the combustion of polluting energy sources. As global temperatures rise, storms can draw more vapor from the oceans, resulting in heavier rainfall, stronger winds, and elevated flooding threats. In contrast, some regions endure severe droughts and associated wildfires.

