The Insurance Council of Australia warns that failing to implement measures to mitigate weather events will lead to an increasing divide between individuals who possess sufficient insurance coverage and those who do not. Enhanced land use strategies and targeted investment in strengthening resilience are imperative to mitigate the impact of weather-related events and protect communities.
